cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "skewbench: a reproducible benchmark for Spark skewed-join mitigation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Malviya
    given-names: Aditya
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-18
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  skewbench is a reproducible harness for evaluating skewed-join mitigation
  strategies in Apache Spark. It generates Zipfian-skewed synthetic workloads
  with an aerospace engine-telemetry schema, executes six join strategies
  (baseline, AQE, uniform salting, selective salting, AQE+salting, broadcast),
  and collects hardware-independent metrics from the Spark event log. It also
  implements an analytical salt-cardinality cost model with a closed-form
  optimum.
